* APOLLO 8 AS FLOWN: A VIEW-1108 SCENARIO (A RUN DECK, IN 1969 TERMS).
*
* The mission as flown, from the post-flight reports.  Card types and units as
* in ../apollo11/asflown.scn (its header lists them); the mission's name,
* range zero and pad are in mission.scn beside this file.
* VIEW made Apollo 8 views:
* "Preflight views produced for the Apollo 8 mission included views as seen
* through the spacecraft windows during various critical maneuvers of the
* flight" (TN D-6853, printed p. 3).  None of them survive; the scene built on
* this scenario uses the formats of the Apollo 11 note, MSC IN 69-FM-197.
*
* Sources:
*   MR8  Apollo 8 Mission Report, MSC-PA-R-69-1, February 1969
*        https://ntrs.nasa.gov/api/citations/19700033031/downloads/19700033031.pdf
*        (printed page numbers).  Table 5-I (p. 5-6): latitudes geodetic for
*        the Earth, selenographic for the Moon; flight-path angle and heading
*        space-fixed.
*   SP   R. W. Orloff, Apollo by the Numbers, NASA SP-2000-4029 (printed pages).
*   SVS  NASA Scientific Visualization Studio 4129, "Earthrise" (E. Wright,
*        A. Chaikin, 2013), https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/4129: the spacecraft's
*        position in its head-up display for each Earthrise frame.
*
SCENARIO ID=1 NAME="AS FLOWN"
*
* The powered ascent, as Apollo 11's: SP p. 45's ascent table, lift-off to
* S-IVB first cutoff.
LEG TYPE=TABLE LATTYPE=GC SRC="SP p. 45, Apollo 8 ascent phase table: geocentric latitude, altitude, space-fixed velocity, flight-path angle and heading"
ROW T=0:00:00.67 LAT=28.4470 LON=-80.6041 ALT=0.032 V=1340.7 FPA=0.00 HDG=90.00 SRC="SP p. 45, liftoff"
ROW T=0:01:01.45 LAT=28.4526 LON=-80.5805 ALT=3.971 V=2078.4 FPA=26.79 HDG=85.21 SRC="SP p. 45, Mach 1 achieved"
ROW T=0:01:18.9 LAT=28.4645 LON=-80.5398 ALT=7.252 V=2754.7 FPA=29.56 HDG=82.43 SRC="SP p. 45, maximum dynamic pressure"
ROW T=0:02:05.93 LAT=28.5581 LON=-80.1934 ALT=22.398 V=6213.78 FPA=24.527 HDG=76.572 SRC="SP p. 45, S-IC center engine cutoff"
ROW T=0:02:33.82 LAT=28.6856 LON=-79.7302 ALT=35.503 V=8899.77 FPA=20.699 HDG=75.387 SRC="SP p. 45, S-IC outboard engine cutoff"
ROW T=0:02:34.47 LAT=28.6893 LON=-79.7168 ALT=35.838 V=8930.15 FPA=20.605 HDG=75.384 SRC="SP p. 45, S-IC/S-II separation"
ROW T=0:08:44.04 LAT=31.5492 LON=-65.3897 ALT=103.424 V=22379.1 FPA=0.646 HDG=81.777 SRC="SP p. 45, S-II engine cutoff"
ROW T=0:08:44.90 LAT=31.5565 LON=-65.3338 ALT=103.460 V=22391.60 FPA=0.636 HDG=81.807 SRC="SP p. 45, S-II/S-IVB separation"
ROW T=0:11:24.98 LAT=32.4541 LON=-54.0565 ALT=103.324 V=25562.43 FPA=-0.001 HDG=88.098 SRC="SP p. 45, S-IVB 1st burn cutoff"
*
* Earth parking orbit, as Apollo 11's: the S-IVB first cutoff state on a
* circle at the mean of SP's 99.99 by 99.57 n mi (p. 45), from that cutoff.
LEG TYPE=CIRC FROM=0:11:24.98 TO=2:50:37.79 T=0:11:24.98 LATTYPE=GC LAT=32.4541 LON=-54.0565 V=25562.43 FPA=-0.001 HDG=88.098 ALT=99.78 SRC="SP p. 45 ascent table, S-IVB 1st burn cutoff: geocentric 32.4541 N, -54.0565 E, space-fixed velocity 25,562.43, flight-path angle -0.001, heading 88.098; orbit 99.99 by 99.57 n mi, same page"
*
* Translunar coast: conics from translunar injection and from the first
* midcourse correction cutoff.  Earth only (no lunar gravity): ours.
LEG TYPE=CONIC FROM=2:56:05.5 TO=10:59:59.5 T=2:56:05.5 LATTYPE=GD LAT=21.48 LON=-143.02 ALT=187.1 V=35505 FPA=7.90 HDG=67.49 SRC="MR8 Table 5-II p. 5-7, translunar injection"
LEG TYPE=CONIC FROM=10:59:59.5 TO=69:08:20.4 T=11:00:01.9 LATTYPE=GD LAT=-1.71 LON=-123.75 ALT=52771.7 V=8172 FPA=73.75 HDG=120.54 SRC="MR8 Table 5-II p. 5-7, first midcourse correction cutoff"
*
* Lunar orbit.  After insertion, the 168.5 by 60.0 n mi ellipse (MR8 p. 5-3)
* on a circle through the insertion cutoff and circularization ignition rows
* at the mean altitude, two revolutions apart ("About two revolutions later",
* same page): ours, as Apollo 11's.  After circularization (60.7 by 59.7 n
* mi, MR8 p. 5-3), a circle through the Earthrise photograph's position and
* the transearth injection ignition row, six whole revolutions between them
* (the ten of MR8 p. 5-3 end at TEI; the count is ours, from the 7,140 s
* period); its altitude is the SVS position's 110.0 km (59.40 n mi) above the
* mean radius, near MR8's 60.2 mean.
LEG TYPE=LUNAR FROM=69:08:20.4 TO=73:35:07 T=69:12:27.3 LAT=-9.89 LON=179.56 TB=73:35:07 LATB=-11.61 LONB=160.29 N=2 ALT=114.25 SRC="MR8 Table 5-II p. 5-7, lunar orbit insertion cutoff and circularization ignition; altitude the mean of MR8 p. 5-3's 168.5 by 60.0 n mi"
LEG TYPE=LUNAR FROM=73:35:07 TO=89:19:16.6 T=75:48:39.7 LAT=-11.15 LON=113.80 TB=89:19:16.6 LATB=-9.27 LONB=174.78 N=6 ALT=59.40 SRC="SVS 4129, head-up display at AS08-14-2383 (16:39:39.7 UT = 75:48:39.7 g.e.t.): 11.15 S, 113.80 E, 110.0 km; MR8 Table 5-II p. 5-8, transearth injection ignition"
*
* Transearth coast: conics from the third midcourse correction ignition and
* from entry interface, to entry interface.  Earth only: ours.
LEG TYPE=CONIC FROM=89:22:40.3 TO=103:59:54 T=103:59:54 LATTYPE=GD LAT=-5.67 LON=-57.27 ALT=165561.5 V=4299 FPA=-80.59 HDG=52.65 SRC="MR8 Table 5-II p. 5-8, third midcourse correction ignition"
LEG TYPE=CONIC FROM=103:59:54 TO=146:46:12.8 T=146:46:12.8 LATTYPE=GD LAT=20.83 LON=-179.89 ALT=65.90 V=36221 FPA=-6.50 HDG=121.57 SRC="MR8 Table 5-V p. 5-10, entry interface (400 000 feet); the table prints the flight-path angle unsigned, 6.50, and entry is downward"
*
* Entry, entry interface to splashdown.  Between them, three states of the
* best-estimate trajectory, MR8 Table 6.9-IV p. 6-52 (peak g, start of the
* final phase, drogue deployment minus 50 s: X, Y, Z in ft and ft/s, the
* Z axis the Earth's (their latitudes match Table 5-V's at entry interface
* and at the drogues to 0.02 deg)), made into these rows by us: placed on
* the turning Earth from Table 5-V's entry interface longitude.  So placed
* the drogue-minus-50 s state lies 3.217 deg of longitude east of Table
* 5-V's drogue position (8.100 N, 165.013 W, best estimate), which no
* 50 s fall closes; we take that up by turning the rows west at a steady
* rate from entry interface to it (positions only), so the third lands on
* the drogue longitude.  Under the parachutes the CM falls straight down
* (ours); after splashdown it rides at the splash point.
LEG TYPE=TABLE LATTYPE=GD SRC="Apollo 8 entry: MR8 Tables 5-V p. 5-10, 6.9-IV p. 6-52 and 3-I p. 3-4"
ROW T=146:46:12.8 LAT=20.83 LON=-179.89 ALT=65.90 V=36221 FPA=-6.50 HDG=121.57 SRC="MR8 Table 5-V p. 5-10, entry interface (400 000 feet)"
ROW T=146:47:38.4 LAT=16.445 LON=-173.657 ALT=30.006 V=31288.2 FPA=-0.087 HDG=123.411 SRC="MR8 Table 6.9-IV p. 6-52, peak g, best-estimate trajectory, made a row by us (see above)"
ROW T=146:48:34.4 LAT=14.092 LON=-170.696 ALT=31.816 V=24881.5 FPA=-0.817 HDG=124.580 SRC="MR8 Table 6.9-IV p. 6-52, start of the final phase, best-estimate trajectory, made a row by us (see above)"
ROW T=146:53:56.4 LAT=8.118 LON=-165.013 ALT=8.426 V=1842.8 FPA=-18.777 HDG=100.034 SRC="MR8 Table 6.9-IV p. 6-52, drogue deployment minus 50 seconds, best-estimate trajectory, made a row by us (see above)"
ROW T=146:54:47.8 LAT=8.100 LON=-165.013 ALT=3.785 V=300 FPA=-90 HDG=0 VEL=EF SRC="MR8 Table 3-I p. 3-4, drogue deployment; position MR8 Table 5-V p. 5-10, best-estimate trajectory; 23,000 ft (3.785 n mi), Apollo 8 Flight Journal, day 6, PAO at 146:53:57: Drogue chutes out at 23,000 feet; falling at 300 ft/s, ours"
ROW T=146:55:38.9 LAT=8.100 LON=-165.013 ALT=1.646 V=30 FPA=-90 HDG=0 VEL=EF SRC="MR8 Table 3-I p. 3-4, main parachute deployment; 10,000 ft (1.646 n mi), ours, from the crew's Should be approaching 10K ... Standby with the mains in 1 second, Apollo 8 Flight Journal, day 6, 146:55:32; then about 30 ft/s, the mean fall from there to the water"
ROW T=147:00:42 LAT=8.125 LON=-165.020 ALT=0 V=31 FPA=-90 HDG=0 VEL=EF SRC="MR8 Table 3-I p. 3-4, landing; MR8 p. 9-4, 8 deg 7.5 min N, 165 deg 1.2 min W (recovery forces); splashdown at 31 ft/s on three parachutes, Apollo 11 press kit printed p. 62"
*
* Events.
EVENT KIND=TLI T=2:56:05.5 SRC="MR8 Table 5-II p. 5-7, translunar injection (cutoff 2:55:55.5 plus 10 s)"
EVENT KIND=SEP T=3:20:59.3 SRC="MR8 Table 3-I p. 3-3, spacecraft/S-IVB separation"
* No EJECT event (no LM, no docking), so the S-IVB has no state after SEP
* (traj.f SIVST).  The CSM kept station with it, then made two RCS
* separation manoeuvres, 1.1 ft/s at 3:40:01 and 7.7 ft/s at 4:45:01 (MR8
* p. 5-2), both radially outward (Apollo 8 Flight Journal, commentary at
* 003:40 and Borman at 004:45:54); the crew's ranges, "between 500 to
* 1,000 feet" at 003:58:48, "about 1,000 feet" at 004:50:45 and "about
* 3,000 feet" at 004:55:46 (same), do not follow from those two burns on
* straight lines (we tried: 1,240, 7,300 and 10,000 ft from SEP), and the
* range at SEP is not given.
EVENT KIND=LOI1 T=69:08:20.4 SRC="MR8 Table 3-I p. 3-3, lunar orbit insertion ignition"
EVENT KIND=LOI2 T=73:35:07 SRC="MR8 Table 3-I p. 3-3, lunar orbit circularization ignition"
EVENT KIND=PHOTO T=75:48:39.7 SRC="SVS 4129: AS08-14-2383, the Earthrise photograph, at 16:39:39.7 UT on 24 December 1968, which is 75:48:39.7 after range zero"
EVENT KIND=TEI T=89:19:16.6 SRC="MR8 Table 3-I p. 3-3, transearth injection ignition"
* The launch vehicle's stages (vdrive.f LVPL, ASCPL; #97), as for Apollo 11.
EVENT KIND=LIFTOFF T=0:00:00.67 SRC="SP p. 47, Liftoff (umbilical disconnected) 000:00:00.67"
EVENT KIND=SICSEP T=0:02:34.47 SRC="SP p. 47, S-IC maximum Earth-fixed velocity; S-IC/S-II separation command 000:02:34.47"
EVENT KIND=LESJET T=0:03:08.6 SRC="SP p. 47, Launch escape tower jettisoned 000:03:08.6"
EVENT KIND=SIISEP T=0:08:44.90 SRC="SP p. 47, S-II maximum Earth-fixed velocity; S-II/S-IVB separation command 000:08:44.90"
EVENT KIND=CMSEP T=146:28:48.0 SRC="SP p. 50, CM/SM separation"
EVENT KIND=EI T=146:46:12.8 SRC="MR8 Table 3-I p. 3-4, entry interface (400 000 feet)"
*
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
* TIMELINE: the mission's sequence of events as SP-4029 prints it (printed pp. 47-50, "Apollo 8 Timeline"),
* one card per row, in the book's order, for chapter marks and the scenes
* to key on.  T is the book's g.e.t. (negative before range zero), NAME its
* wording (OCR slips mended, quotation marks made ', cut to 60 characters
* with ...), SRC its page.  KIND is ours, one of (CLAUDE.md, "Scenario
* timeline"): LAUNCH countdown, lift-off and ascent flight; BURN a firing,
* ignition or cutoff (S-IVB, SPS, RCS, LM); STAGING launch-vehicle stage
* events (engine cutoffs, separations, jettisons, apex, impact); ORBIT
* orbit and trajectory milestones; SEP spacecraft separation, docking,
* undocking, ejection, jettison; SURFACE on the Moon, landing to lunar
* lift-off; TV television; CREW crew and CAPCOM words, crew movements;
* PHOTO photography and sightings; ENTRY entry, landing and recovery; MARK
* anything else (systems, communications, venting).  The EVENT cards above
* stay the kernel's keys.
*
TIMELINE T=-028:00:00 KIND=LAUNCH NAME="Terminal countdown started" SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=-009:00:00 KIND=LAUNCH NAME="Scheduled 6-hour hold at T-9 hours" SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=-009:00:00 KIND=LAUNCH NAME="Countdown resumed at T-9 hours" SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=-003:30:00 KIND=LAUNCH NAME="Scheduled 1-hour hold at T-3 hours 30 minutes" SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=-003:30:00 KIND=LAUNCH NAME="Countdown resumed at T-3 hours 30 minutes" SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=-002:53 KIND=LAUNCH NAME="Crew ingress" SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=-000:00:16.970 KIND=LAUNCH NAME="Guidance reference release" SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=-000:00:08.89 KIND=LAUNCH NAME="S-IC engine start command" SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=-000:00:06.585 KIND=LAUNCH NAME="S-IC engine ignition (#5)" SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=-000:00:01.387 KIND=LAUNCH NAME="All S-IC engines thrust OK" SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=000:00:00.00 KIND=LAUNCH NAME="Range zero" SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=000:00:00.27 KIND=LAUNCH NAME="All holddown arms released" SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=000:00:00.33 KIND=LAUNCH NAME="1st motion (1.16 g)" SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=000:00:00.67 KIND=LAUNCH NAME="Liftoff (umbilical disconnected)" SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=000:00:01.76 KIND=LAUNCH NAME="Tower clearance yaw maneuver started" SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=000:00:09.72 KIND=LAUNCH NAME="Yaw maneuver ended" SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=000:00:12.11 KIND=LAUNCH NAME="Pitch and roll maneuver started" SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=000:00:31.52 KIND=LAUNCH NAME="Roll maneuver ended" SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=000:01:01.45 KIND=LAUNCH NAME="Mach 1 achieved" SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=000:01:14.7 KIND=LAUNCH NAME="Maximum bending moment achieved (60,000,000 lbf-in)" SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=000:01:18.9 KIND=LAUNCH NAME="Maximum dynamic pressure (776.938 lb/ft2)" SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=000:02:05.93 KIND=STAGING NAME="S-IC center engine cutoff command" SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=000:02:25.50 KIND=LAUNCH NAME="Pitch maneuver ended" SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=000:02:33.82 KIND=STAGING NAME="S-IC outboard engine cutoff" SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=000:02:33.92 KIND=STAGING NAME="S-IC maximum total inertial acceleration (3.96 g)" SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=000:02:34.47 KIND=STAGING NAME="S-IC maximum Earth-fixed velocity; S-IC/S-II separation..." SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=000:02:35.19 KIND=STAGING NAME="S-II engine start command" SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=000:02:36.19 KIND=STAGING NAME="S-II ignition" SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=000:03:04.47 KIND=STAGING NAME="S-II aft interstage jettisoned" SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=000:03:08.6 KIND=STAGING NAME="Launch escape tower jettisoned" SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=000:03:16.22 KIND=LAUNCH NAME="Iterative guidance mode initiated" SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=000:04:26.54 KIND=STAGING NAME="S-IC apex" SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=000:08:44.04 KIND=STAGING NAME="S-II engine cutoff" SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=000:08:44.14 KIND=STAGING NAME="S-II maximum total inertial acceleration (1.86 g)" SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=000:08:44.90 KIND=STAGING NAME="S-II maximum Earth-fixed velocity; S-II/S-IVB separation..." SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=000:08:45.00 KIND=MARK NAME="S-IVB 1st burn start command" SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=000:08:48.29 KIND=BURN NAME="S-IVB 1st burn ignition" SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=000:08:56.8 KIND=STAGING NAME="S-IVB ullage case jettisoned" SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=000:09:00.41 KIND=STAGING NAME="S-IC impact (theoretical)" SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=000:09:20.34 KIND=STAGING NAME="S-II apex" SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=000:11:24.98 KIND=BURN NAME="S-IVB 1st burn cutoff" SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=000:11:25.08 KIND=MARK NAME="S-IVB 1st burn maximum total inertial acceleration (0.72 g)" SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=000:11:25.50 KIND=MARK NAME="S-IVB 1st burn maximum Earth-fixed velocity" SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=000:11:34.98 KIND=ORBIT NAME="Earth orbit insertion" SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=000:11:45.19 KIND=ORBIT NAME="Maneuver to local horizontal attitude started" SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=000:13:05.19 KIND=ORBIT NAME="Orbital navigation started" SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=000:19:25.106 KIND=STAGING NAME="S-II impact (theoretical)" SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=000:42:05 KIND=MARK NAME="Optics cover jettisoned" SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=001:56:00 KIND=MARK NAME="All spacecraft systems approved for translunar injection" SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=002:27:22 KIND=CREW NAME="CAPCOM (Collins); 'All right, Apollo 8. You are go for TLI.'" SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=002:40:59.54 KIND=MARK NAME="S-IVB 2nd burn restart preparation" SRC="SP p. 47"
TIMELINE T=002:50:29.51 KIND=MARK NAME="S-IVB 2nd burn restart command" SRC="SP p. 48"
TIMELINE T=002:50:37.79 KIND=BURN NAME="S-IVB 2nd burn ignition" SRC="SP p. 48"
TIMELINE T=002:55:55.51 KIND=BURN NAME="S-IVB 2nd burn cutoff" SRC="SP p. 48"
TIMELINE T=002:55:55.61 KIND=MARK NAME="S-IVB 2nd burn maximum total inertial acceleration (1.55 g)" SRC="SP p. 48"
TIMELINE T=002:55:55.91 KIND=MARK NAME="S-IVB LH2 tank latch relief valve open" SRC="SP p. 48"
TIMELINE T=002:55:56.00 KIND=MARK NAME="S-IVB 2nd burn maximum Earth-fixed velocity" SRC="SP p. 48"
TIMELINE T=002:55:56.19 KIND=MARK NAME="S-IVB LH2 tank CVS valve open" SRC="SP p. 48"
TIMELINE T=002:55:56.19 KIND=MARK NAME="S-IVB sating procedures started" SRC="SP p. 48"
TIMELINE T=002:55:56.42 KIND=MARK NAME="S-IVB LOX tank non-propulsive vent valve open" SRC="SP p. 48"
TIMELINE T=002:56:05.51 KIND=ORBIT NAME="Translunar injection" SRC="SP p. 48"
TIMELINE T=002:56:15.77 KIND=ORBIT NAME="Maneuver to local horizontal attitude and orbital..." SRC="SP p. 48"
TIMELINE T=002:58:26.39 KIND=MARK NAME="S-IVB LOX tank non-propulsive vent valve closed" SRC="SP p. 48"
TIMELINE T=003:10:55.71 KIND=MARK NAME="S-IVB LH2 tank CVS valve and tank relief valve closed" SRC="SP p. 48"
TIMELINE T=003:10:58.40 KIND=MARK NAME="Maneuver to transposition and docking attitude started" SRC="SP p. 48"
TIMELINE T=003:20:56.3 KIND=MARK NAME="Sequence to separate CSM from S-IVB/LTA started..." SRC="SP p. 48"
TIMELINE T=003:20:59.3 KIND=SEP NAME="CSM separated from S-IVB" SRC="SP p. 48"
TIMELINE T=003:40:01 KIND=BURN NAME="1st CSM evasive maneuver from S-IVB (RCS)" SRC="SP p. 48"
TIMELINE T=003:55:56.16 KIND=MARK NAME="S-IVB LH2 tank latch relief valve open" SRC="SP p. 48"
TIMELINE T=004:10:55.77 KIND=MARK NAME="S-IVB LH2 tank latch relief valve closed" SRC="SP p. 48"
TIMELINE T=004:39:54 KIND=MARK NAME="Last reported VHF uplink reception" SRC="SP p. 48"
TIMELINE T=004:44:56.63 KIND=MARK NAME="S-IVB lunar slingshot attitude maneuver initiated" SRC="SP p. 48"
TIMELINE T=004:45:01 KIND=BURN NAME="2nd CSM evasive maneuver from S-IVB (RCS)" SRC="SP p. 48"
TIMELINE T=004:48 KIND=MARK NAME="Last reported VHF downlink reception" SRC="SP p. 48"
TIMELINE T=004:55:56.02 KIND=MARK NAME="S-IVB LH2 tank CVS valve open" SRC="SP p. 48"
TIMELINE T=004:55:56.02 KIND=MARK NAME="S-IVB lunar slingshot maneuver-LH2 vent valve open command" SRC="SP p. 48"
